[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 1:27] Understood. What is the biggest risk to your recommendation, and how would you mitigate it?

[candidate · 2:05] The biggest risk is that my 24% number is derived from accounting, not from customer behavior. I backed into it by solving for a 24% margin at constant volume — but constant volume is exactly the assumption a 24% price increase puts under pressure. If elasticity is even moderately negative, say volume drops 10%, I lose a meaningful chunk of the recovery and I've also damaged traffic, which is the one healthy thing in this business.

There's a specific wrinkle too: ticket is up because people are buying more items per visit. Multi-item baskets are more price-sensitive in aggregate — the second pastry is the first thing to go. So I could see ticket compress even if transactions hold.

Mitigation: test before scaling. Pilot in two or three comparable markets for 8–12 weeks, measure transactions and items-per-basket separately, and set a stop-gate — if traffic falls more than 3–4%, pause and shift weight to mix and supply-side levers instead.
